    "1": {
      "purpose": "STR for Telemetry Acquisition Subsystem\n\nPurpose: This System Requirement Specification (SRS) defines the system-level requirements for the telemetry acquisition subsystem of [Project Name]. The purpose of this software is to acquire and process real-time telemetry data from various sensor channels, enabling critical mission operations in a defense environment.  The system will support existing parent systems by providing reliable and timely access to critical operational data.\n\nScope: This SRS focuses on the high-level requirements for the telemetry acquisition subsystem. It does not cover:\nDetailed design or implementation details (e.g., specific sensor types, data processing algorithms, or REST API implementation details).\n\nTest Strategy:  This document outlines the test strategy for the Defence R&D software project, aligning with the functional requirements outlined in the System Requirement Specification (SRS). The testing approach will be based on a combination of:\nFunctional Testing: This will involve verifying that each functional requirement is met as defined in the SRS (REQ-0001, REQ-0002, etc.). This includes unit testing, integration testing, and system testing.\n\nBounded Buffering: The system shall expose acquired samples through a REST interface to the ground segment.  The system shall implement bounded buffering for time-tagged data.\nEngineering Log: The system shall record an engineering log with a minimum depth of 6 months of mission operations.\n\nNote: This document outlines the high-level requirements for the telemetry acquisition subsystem and does not cover detailed design or implementation details.  The test strategy will ensure the software meets its intended functionality and performance objectives throughout development and deployment.",
      "scope": "STR - Scope\n\nIntroduction\n\nThis Software Requirements Specification (STR) outlines the scope of the Defence R&D software project.  The project aims to develop [State Project Goal] using [Mention Technology/Methodology].\n\nScope\n\nThe project's scope encompasses the following:\n\nTest Items: Two test items will be developed and implemented within this project (REQ-0001, REQ-0002).\nFeatures: The two test items will include [List specific features].\nProject Scope:  The project's scope is defined by the following: [Specify Project Boundaries]\n\nNote: This document will be updated as the project progresses and new requirements are identified.",
