      "analysis": "STR - Defects and Anomalies Analysis\n\nDefects and Anomalies Analysis\n\nThis section outlines the analysis of defects and anomalies identified during the design review process for the telemetry acquisition subsystem preliminary design.\n\nAnalysis:\n\nRequirement Discrepancies: The initial design did not explicitly define the sampling rate for each channel (REQ-0001). This discrepancy was addressed through a decision at the Design Review 04, where it was decided that the acquisition subsystem shall use a time-tagged sample buffer for all channels.\nREST Interface Versioning: The REST interface in REQ-0005 will be versioned from day one to ensure consistent and reliable data access (REQ-0001).\nAction Items: Several action items were identified during the review, including:\n    * Clarifying Sampling Rate: Update SysRS section 2 to clarify the sampling rate for REQ-0001. This action is assigned to Dr. Sharma and is due on 2026-09-01.\n    * Authentication Mechanism Confirmation: Confirm the authentication mechanism with the security panel with Lt. Rao, due on 2026-09-15.\nRequirement Modifications: The following requirements were modified during the review:\n    * REQ-0006 was modified to require structured JSON logging output.\n    * A new requirement, REQ-0011, was added to specify automatic fault recovery within 30 seconds in addition to REQ-0009.\n\nTest Outcomes:\nREQ-0001: All three channels acquired during the hardware-in-loop demonstration (PASS).\nREQ-0005: The sample retrieval endpoint did not meet latency budget during load test, resulting in a FAIL outcome.\nREQ-0002: MTBF estimate recorded above 2000 hours on the reference platform (PASS).\n\nNotes:\n\nThis analysis will be updated as new information becomes available and defects are identified."
    },
